const String mcpUiDslWidgetsSchemaJson = '{"\$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","\$id":"https://specs.makemind.ai/mcp_ui_dsl/1.4/widgets.schema.json","title":"MCP UI DSL 1.4 — Widget Registry (Phase 1)","\$defs":{"EdgeInsets":{"anyOf":[{"type":"number"},{"type":"object","properties":{"value":{"type":"number"},"unit":{"type":"string"}},"required":["value"]},{"type":"object","properties":{"all":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Dimension"},"horizontal":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Dimension"},"vertical":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Dimension"},"top":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Dimension"},"right":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Dimension"},"bottom":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Dimension"},"left":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Dimension"}}},{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Binding"}],"description":"Space around or inside a box. Four spellings, all accepted wherever insets\\nare expected:\\n\\n- **Number** — one value applied to every edge.\\n- **`{value, unit}`** — the legacy v1.0 dimension object; `unit` is\\n  informational and the runtime treats every inset as logical pixels.\\n- **Edge map** — `{all}` for every edge, `{horizontal, vertical}` for the\\n  two axes, or `{top, right, bottom, left}` for individual edges. Each entry\\n  is a `Dimension`, so one edge may be bound while its neighbours are\\n  literal: `{ \\"left\\": \\"{{sidebar.width}}\\", \\"top\\": 8 }`.\\n- **Binding** — resolves to any of the above at render time.\\n\\nA bare word is not an inset: the runtime resolves it to null and the widget\\nfalls back to no padding, so validators reject it rather than let it render\\nas a silent zero."},"Binding":{"type":"string","pattern":"^\\\\{\\\\{.*\\\\}\\\\}\$","description":"Binding-expression string of the form `\\"{{...}}\\"`. Authors may\\nsubstitute any primitive value with a binding so the runtime\\nresolves the value at render time. Used as an alternative branch\\nin primitives that otherwise expect a specific structural shape\\n(AssetRef, Dimension, BorderRadius, Alignment, …)."},"Origin":{"type":"object","properties":{"connection":{"oneOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"string","pattern":"^\\\\{\\\\{.*\\\\}\\\\}\$"}],"description":"Outbound MCP client connection id, or a binding to one."}},"required":["connection"],"additionalProperties":false,"description":"Who serves a definition. Deliberately open so future sources need no new\\nsyntax — today one shape is defined; `{ \\"bundle\\": ... }` / `{ \\"agent\\": ... }`\\nand similar can be added without changing any document that uses it.\\n\\n`connection` names a live connection in the host\'s outbound MCP client\\nregistry, addressed by the id used to open it. The DSL does not define how\\nconnections are made — that is a host capability (`06_Runtime_Contract.md`\\n§6.11.1); it defines only how a definition is addressed once one exists.\\n\\nA binding is the normal value here: an application opens its connections in\\n`lifecycle.onInit` and keeps the ids in state.\\n\\nRuntimes MUST reject an Origin whose sole key they do not recognise rather\\nthan falling back to the current origin — a permissive reading would render a\\ndifferent server\'s UI under the requested one\'s identity (`07_Security.md`\\n§7.10.1)."},"DefinitionSource":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string","pattern":"^\\\\{\\\\{.*\\\\}\\\\}\$","description":"Binding to a definition held in state (since v1.4)."},{"type":"string","description":"Resource URI on the current origin, e.g. `ui://pages/main`."},{"type":"object","description":"Qualified reference to a definition on another origin (since v1.4).","properties":{"\$ref":{"type":"string","description":"Resource URI to read from the named origin."},"from":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Origin"}},"required":["\$ref"],"additionalProperties":false},{"type":"object","description":"Inline PageDefinition or WidgetDefinition."}],"description":"Where a definition comes from. Four forms: an inline definition, a resource\\nURI on the current origin, a qualified `{ \$ref, from }` reference to another\\norigin, or a binding to a definition already held in state.\\n\\nOmitting `from` means the current origin, so every pre-1.4 document keeps its\\nexact meaning. Naming an origin makes that origin ambient for the resolved\\nsubtree — its tool calls, resource reads, state, storage and permissions all\\nscope to it. See `01_Core_Concepts.md` §1.9 and `07_Security.md` §7.10.\\n\\nAccepted wherever `RouteValue` is accepted (§1.2.1) and as the `source` of the\\n`view` widget (§2.13.1)."},"Color":{"oneOf":[{"type":"string","pattern":"^#([0-9a-fA-F]{3}|[0-9a-fA-F]{6}|[0-9a-fA-F]{8})\$","description":"Hex — `#RGB`, `#RRGGBB`, or `#AARRGGBB` (alpha first)."},{"description":"Material 3 scheme slot (§5.3) — adapts to light / dark mode.","enum":["primary","onPrimary","primaryContainer","onPrimaryContainer","secondary","onSecondary","secondaryContainer","onSecondaryContainer","tertiary","onTertiary","tertiaryContainer","onTertiaryContainer","error","onError","errorContainer","onErrorContainer","surface","onSurface","onSurfaceVariant","surfaceTint","surfaceBright","surfaceDim","surfaceContainerLowest","surfaceContainerLow","surfaceContainer","surfaceContainerHigh","surfaceContainerHighest","outline","outlineVariant","inverseSurface","onInverseSurface","inverseOnSurface","background","onBackground","surfaceVariant","inversePrimary","scrim","shadow","success","onSuccess","warning","onWarning","info","onInfo","divider","foreground","textOnPrimary","textOnSecondary","textOnBackground","textOnSurface","textOnError"],"x-legacy":["divider","foreground","textOnPrimary","textOnSecondary","textOnBackground","textOnSurface","textOnError"],"x-legacy-note":"Pre-M3 slot names (§17.3). Accepted so documents written before §5.3.1\'s roles keep loading and painting; §5.3.1 lists what to write now."},{"type":"string","pattern":"^([Rr][Ee][Dd]|[Bb][Ll][Uu][Ee]|[Gg][Rr][Ee][Ee][Nn]|[Yy][Ee][Ll][Ll][Oo][Ww]|[Oo][Rr][Aa][Nn][Gg][Ee]|[Pp][Uu][Rr][Pp][Ll][Ee]|[Bb][Ll][Aa][Cc][Kk]|[Ww][Hh][Ii][Tt][Ee]|[Gg][Rr][Ee][Yy]|[Gg][Rr][Aa][Yy])\$","description":"CSS basic color name. Spelled as a character class per\\nletter because JSON Schema regexes are ECMA-262, which has no\\ninline `(?i:)` flag — writing one makes the whole branch\\nunconstrained instead of case-insensitive, and it accepted every\\nstring."},{"type":"string","pattern":"^[Rr][Gg][Bb][Aa]? *\\\\( *[0-9]{1,3} *, *[0-9]{1,3} *, *[0-9]{1,3} *(, *([01]|[01]?[.][0-9]+) *)?\\\\) *\$","description":"Functional notation — `rgb(r, g, b)` or `rgba(r, g, b, a)`,\\nchannels 0-255 and alpha 0-1. §5.3.4 rates it SHOULD, below hex:\\nit carries no alpha in the three-channel form and does not adapt\\nto light / dark mode the way a scheme slot does."},{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Binding"}],"description":"A color value. Three spellings, all accepted wherever a color is\\nexpected:\\n\\n- **Hex** — `#RGB`, `#RRGGBB`, or `#AARRGGBB`. The 8-digit form puts\\n  alpha **first**, matching the runtime\'s parse order.\\n- **Theme scheme slot** — a bare Material 3 role name from §5.3.1\\n  (`primary`, `onSurfaceVariant`, `error`, …), the three semantic pairs\\n  this spec adds (`success`, `warning`, `info` and their `on*`), and the\\n  four legacy spellings §5.3.1 keeps (`background`, `onBackground`,\\n  `surfaceVariant`, `inverseOnSurface`).\\n  Resolved against the active theme, so it follows light / dark mode.\\n  This is the preferred form: it is the only one that adapts.\\n- **CSS basic name** — the ten colors a document can name without a\\n  theme (`red`, `blue`, `green`, `yellow`, `orange`, `purple`,\\n  `black`, `white`, `grey`/`gray`). Matched case-insensitively.\\n- **Functional** — `rgb(r, g, b)` / `rgba(r, g, b, a)`. §5.3.4 rates\\n  this SHOULD where hex is MUST; it is accepted so that a theme\\n  written in that notation validates, but it adapts to neither mode\\n  nor palette.\\n\\nBindings are accepted in all three positions.\\n\\nA bare word that is neither a scheme slot nor a basic name is **not**\\na color: the runtime resolves it to null and the widget falls back to\\nits default. Validators reject it rather than let it render as a\\nsilent default."},"BorderRadius":{"oneOf":[{"type":"number","minimum":0},{"type":"object","properties":{"topStart":{"type":"number","minimum":0},"topEnd":{"type":"number","minimum":0},"bottomStart":{"type":"number","minimum":0},"bottomEnd":{"type":"number","minimum":0},"all":{"type":"number","minimum":0}},"additionalProperties":false},{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Binding"}],"description":"Per-corner radius value. A bare number applies uniformly to all\\nfour corners; the object form lets each corner take an independent\\nradius. `all` is a shorthand for setting every corner at once and\\nis overridden by individual corner keys.\\n\\nCorner names are **directional** (RTL-aware) per Material 3:\\n\\n- `topStart` — top corner on the leading edge (top-left in LTR,\\n  top-right in RTL).\\n- `topEnd` — top corner on the trailing edge.\\n- `bottomStart` / `bottomEnd` — same convention on the bottom row.\\n\\nThis is the cross-schema canonical for any \\"per-corner radius\\"\\nshape — referenced by `theme.Shape` (M3 shape token sizes) and by\\nthe `BoxDecoration.borderRadius` widget property."},"AssetRef":{"oneOf":[{"type":"string","pattern":"^([A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9+.-]*:|assets/)"},{"type":"object","properties":{"uri":{"type":"string","description":"Resource uri read through MCP `resources/read` on the resolved origin."},"origin":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Origin"}},"required":["uri"],"additionalProperties":false},{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Binding"}],"description":"Reference to an asset (image, font, audio, video, SVG, …).\\n\\nAn asset reference takes one of three shapes: a **scheme-prefixed\\nstring**, an **object** naming a resource and the origin that serves\\nit, or a **binding** that resolves to either at render time.\\n\\n## Known schemes\\n\\nA runtime dispatches the right loader by prefix:\\n\\n- `bundle://<path>` — asset packaged inside the active bundle. Inside\\n  an embedded subtree this is the *embedded* document\'s bundle, not\\n  the embedder\'s (`06_Runtime_Contract.md` §6.11.3).\\n- `https://<url>` / `http://<url>` — fetched over the network and\\n  cached on first render.\\n- `data:<mime>;base64,<payload>` (or `data:<mime>,<urlencoded>`) —\\n  inline bytes carried in the DSL itself. The only form that needs no\\n  I/O capability at all, and so the one a constrained host can always\\n  render.\\n- `assets/<path>` — Flutter-style local asset path declared in the\\n  consumer app\'s pubspec asset list (used by host integrations that\\n  ship icon SVGs alongside the runtime).\\n- `client://<channel>/<id>` — resource served by the client / host\\n  process via an MCP client-extension channel (`08_Client_Extensions.md`\\n  §8.3). This is how a document reaches the *host\'s* own files —\\n  `client://file/…`, `client://workspace/…` — rather than the server\'s.\\n\\n**This list is open, not closed.** The pattern admits any RFC 3986\\nscheme so a host may serve forms this document does not name, exactly\\nas `Origin` admits sources beyond `connection`. A runtime that meets a\\nscheme it does not implement MUST fail visibly per §6.12 rather than\\nreject the document — an author naming a scheme this runtime lacks has\\nwritten a valid document that this runtime cannot fully render, which\\nis not the same as an invalid document.\\n\\n## Object form — an asset served by an origin\\n\\n```json\\n{ \\"uri\\": \\"file:///reports/2026-q2.pdf\\", \\"origin\\": { \\"connection\\": \\"{{ deviceId }}\\" } }\\n```\\n\\n`uri` is read through MCP `resources/read` on the named origin. No new\\nscheme is minted for \\"the server\'s own asset\\": MCP already reads an\\narbitrary resource uri and returns text or base64 `blob`, so a server\\npublishes assets the same way it publishes anything else.\\n\\n`origin` is the `Origin` primitive, so addressing an asset and\\naddressing a definition use one vocabulary. Omitted, the asset resolves\\nagainst the **ambient origin** — the origin of the definition that\\ndeclares it (§6.11.3), never the embedder\'s.\\n\\nThe object form is what lets an asset stay *out* of application state.\\nA server with room can publish a resource uri and let the runtime pull\\nthe bytes; a server without room can inline the same asset as a `data:`\\nstring. Both are valid, and which one a server chooses is its own\\ndecision — the DSL does not force a transport on it.\\n\\n## Support is declared, not assumed\\n\\nRuntimes declare which schemes they resolve (§6.12, §18.9). Nothing\\nhere requires a runtime to implement all of them; it requires a runtime\\nto be honest about which it does, and to route the rest to the\\nconsumer\'s declared fallback instead of a blank box or a placeholder\\nbearing an implementation detail.\\n\\nUsed cross-schema by `app` (splash · publisher logos · font assets),\\n`page`/widgets (image · icon · avatar · lottieAnimation ·\\nBackgroundImage · mediaPlayer · rive · lightbox), and `theme` (font\\nasset registration). Lives under `configs/_primitive/` for that reason."},"Dimension":{"oneOf":[{"type":"number"},{"type":"object","properties":{"value":{"oneOf":[{"type":"number"},{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Binding"}]},"unit":{"type":"string"}},"required":["value"],"additionalProperties":false},{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Binding"},{"type":"object","propertyNames":{"enum":["compact","medium","expanded","large","extraLarge","embedded","default"]},"minProperties":1,"additionalProperties":{"oneOf":[{"type":"number"},{"type":"object","properties":{"value":{"oneOf":[{"type":"number"},{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Binding"}]},"unit":{"type":"string"}},"required":["value"],"additionalProperties":false},{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Binding"}]}}],"description":"Numeric size — accepts a plain `number` (logical pixels) OR the\\nlegacy MCP UI DSL v1.0 `{value, unit}` object form. The `unit`\\nfield is informational; the runtime treats every dimension as\\nlogical pixels. `value` may itself be a binding: a bar whose width\\ncomes from data writes `{\\"value\\": \\"{{item.ratio}}\\", \\"unit\\": \\"percent\\"}`,\\nand that is the whole point of the object form.\\n\\nA responsive object (§14.2.2) — one value per form factor, keyed by\\n`compact` / `medium` / `expanded` / `large` / `extraLarge` / `embedded`\\n/ `default` — stands in for any of those forms."},"Alignment":{"oneOf":[{"enum":["topStart","topLeft","topCenter","topEnd","topRight","centerStart","centerLeft","center","centerEnd","centerRight","bottomStart","bottomLeft","bottomCenter","bottomEnd","bottomRight"]},{"type":"object","properties":{"x":{"type":"number","minimum":-1,"maximum":1},"y":{"type":"number","minimum":-1,"maximum":1}},"required":["x","y"],"additionalProperties":false},{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Binding"}],"description":"2D alignment within a rectangle. Token names are **directional**\\n(RTL-aware) per Material 3:\\n\\n- `topStart` — top corner on the leading edge (top-left in LTR,\\n  top-right in RTL).\\n- `topEnd` — top corner on the trailing edge.\\n- `centerStart` / `centerEnd`, `bottomStart` / `bottomEnd` — same\\n  convention on the middle / bottom rows.\\n- `topCenter`, `center`, `bottomCenter` — neutral on the cross\\n  axis.\\n\\nObject form `{x, y}` is a numeric pair where each axis runs from\\n-1 (start) through 0 (center) to 1 (end). The numeric form\\nsupports any point inside or outside the rectangle.\\n\\nCross-schema canonical for any \\"2D rectangle alignment\\" use —\\nchild placement (`box.alignment`, `align.alignment`,\\n`stack.alignment`), gradient endpoints (`Gradient.begin/end`),\\nimage fit (`BackgroundImage.alignment`)."},"AnimationCurve":{"enum":["linear","easeIn","easeOut","easeInOut","standard","standardAccelerate","standardDecelerate","emphasized","emphasizedAccelerate","emphasizedDecelerate","bounceIn","bounceOut"],"description":"Easing curve applied to an animation\'s progress. Eleven canonical\\nvalues cover the M3-recommended palette plus the CSS-familiar\\nbasics:\\n\\n- **CSS-familiar** — `linear`, `easeIn`, `easeOut`, `easeInOut`.\\n- **M3 standard** — `standard`, `standardAccelerate`,\\n  `standardDecelerate`. Used for everyday transitions; minimal\\n  overshoot, clean cubic.\\n- **M3 emphasized** — `emphasized`, `emphasizedAccelerate`,\\n  `emphasizedDecelerate`. Used for hero / page transitions; more\\n  dramatic acceleration profile.\\n- **Bounce** — `bounceIn`, `bounceOut`. For attention / alert\\n  micro-interactions.\\n\\nCross-schema canonical for `animatedContainer.curve`,\\n`animatedOpacity.curve`, RouteTransition, scrollAnimated easing,\\nand any future implicit-animation widget. Matches the M3 motion\\nspec\'s named tokens 1:1 so theme-level motion overrides stay\\nvendor-neutral."},"Gradient":{"type":"object","properties":{"type":{"enum":["linear","radial","sweep"]},"colors":{"type":"array","items":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Color"},"minItems":2},"stops":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"number","minimum":0,"maximum":1}},"begin":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Alignment"},"end":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Alignment"},"center":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Alignment"},"radius":{"type":"number","minimum":0},"startAngle":{"type":"number"},"endAngle":{"type":"number"},"tileMode":{"enum":["clamp","repeated","mirror"],"default":"clamp"}},"required":["type","colors"],"additionalProperties":false,"description":"Multi-stop gradient fill. Selected by `type`:\\n\\n- `linear` — straight axis from `begin` (default `centerLeft`) to\\n  `end` (default `centerRight`).\\n- `radial` — circular gradient out from `center` (default `center`)\\n  to `radius` (default `0.5`, expressed as a fraction of the\\n  bounding rectangle\'s longest side).\\n- `sweep` — angular gradient around `center`, swept from\\n  `startAngle` (default `0`) to `endAngle` (default `2π`) in\\n  radians.\\n\\n`colors` lists at least two color values; `stops` (optional) places\\neach color at a position in `[0, 1]`. `tileMode` controls behaviour\\npast the gradient extents."},"BackgroundImage":{"type":"object","properties":{"image":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/AssetRef"},"fit":{"enum":["fill","contain","cover","fitWidth","fitHeight","none","scaleDown"],"default":"cover"},"alignment":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Alignment"},"opacity":{"type":"number","minimum":0,"maximum":1},"colorFilter":{"type":"object","properties":{"color":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Color"},"blendMode":{"enum":["srcIn","color","screen","overlay","multiply"],"default":"srcIn","description":"Curated subset of blend modes covering the common tinting use cases (`srcIn` for solid tint, `color` for hue swap, `screen`/`overlay`/`multiply` for atmosphere)."}},"required":["color"],"additionalProperties":false},"repeat":{"enum":["noRepeat","repeat","repeatX","repeatY"],"default":"noRepeat"}},"required":["image"],"additionalProperties":false,"description":"Image fill behind a box\'s content. `image` accepts the same forms as\\nthe `image` widget\'s `src` (`bundle://`, `https?://`, `data:`,\\n`client://`). `fit` and `alignment` mirror the `image` widget\'s\\nsemantics. `opacity` applies an alpha multiplier; `colorFilter`\\ncomposites a tint via the named blend mode. `repeat` controls\\ntiling behaviour outside the image\'s natural bounds."},"RouteTransition":{"type":"object","properties":{"style":{"enum":["slide","fade","scale","cube","sharedAxis","fadeThrough"]},"duration":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Dimension","description":"Total transition duration in milliseconds. Defaults to the M3 motion-system value for the chosen style."},"curve":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/AnimationCurve","description":"Easing curve for the transition\'s progress. Defaults to `emphasized`."},"axis":{"enum":["horizontal","vertical"],"description":"Direction for `slide` / `sharedAxis`. Defaults to `horizontal`."},"reverse":{"type":"boolean","default":false,"description":"When true, run the transition in reverse direction (for back navigation)."}},"required":["style"],"additionalProperties":false,"description":"Per-route page transition. Declared on a `RouteValue` so every\\n`navigate` to that route uses the same transition, OR overridden\\ninline on a `navigate` action. Six canonical styles:\\n\\n- `slide` — incoming page slides over the outgoing along the\\n  direction (M3 default for forward navigation).\\n- `fade` — cross-fade between pages at the same position.\\n- `scale` — outgoing scales out, incoming scales in.\\n- `cube` — perspective-rotate as if turning a 3D cube; needs a\\n  perspective-aware compositor (falls back to `slide` when\\n  unavailable).\\n- `sharedAxis` — coordinated slide+fade across an axis (M3 motion\\n  pattern for sibling-level navigation).\\n- `fadeThrough` — outgoing fades out while incoming fades in\\n  after a brief zero-opacity bridge (M3 motion pattern for\\n  top-level navigation)."},"IconRef":{"\$comment":"anyOf, not oneOf: the name branch is an unconstrained string, so a binding expression matches both it and the Binding branch. `oneOf` reads that legitimate value as a violation — the same reason the Widget union uses anyOf.","anyOf":[{"type":"string","description":"Icon name, or an AssetRef string (scheme-prefixed, or an `assets/` path)."},{"type":"object","properties":{"codepoint":{"type":"integer"},"fontFamily":{"type":"string"},"fontPackage":{"type":"string"}},"required":["codepoint"],"additionalProperties":false},{"type":"object","properties":{"uri":{"type":"string","description":"Resource uri read through MCP `resources/read` on the resolved origin."},"origin":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Origin"}},"required":["uri"],"additionalProperties":false},{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Binding"}],"description":"Reference to an icon. Three forms, all accepted anywhere an icon is\\ntaken — the `icon` widget and every widget with an icon slot\\n(`button.icon`, `iconButton.icon`, `floatingActionButton.icon`,\\n`popupMenuButton.icon`, `rating.icon`, `offlineFallback.icon`,\\n`permissionPrompt.icon`, …):\\n\\n1. **Name** — `\\"home\\"`, `\\"folder_open\\"`, … resolved through the\\n   runtime\'s built-in icon table. Zero-cost, and the default reading of\\n   a bare string.\\n2. **Codepoint** — `{codepoint, fontFamily?, fontPackage?}` for glyphs\\n   the name table does not carry.\\n3. **`AssetRef`** — any form that primitive accepts (network URL,\\n   `bundle://`, `assets/`, `data:image/svg+xml;…`, `client://`, or the\\n   `{uri, origin?}` object). Which of those a runtime resolves is\\n   declared, not assumed (`06_Runtime_Contract.md` §6.12).\\n\\nA bare string carrying a known scheme prefix (or an `assets/` path) is\\nan asset; every other bare string is a **name**. That rule is what lets\\nthe named form stay the zero-ceremony default while the same slot also\\naccepts a server-served glyph.\\n\\nThis primitive exists so the rule is stated once. Before it, `icon`\\ndocumented three forms while the eight other icon slots were typed as\\nbare strings — so the same value was legal in one slot and undeclared\\nin the next, and a codepoint object could not be written at all outside\\nthe `icon` widget."},"NavigationStyle":{"type":"object","properties":{"backgroundColor":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Color"},"backgroundImage":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/BackgroundImage"},"indicatorColor":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Color","description":"Selection indicator pill color (rail / drawer / tabs)."},"indicatorShape":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/BorderRadius","description":"Selection indicator corner radius. Defaults to a fully-rounded pill."},"dividerColor":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Color","description":"Drawer-only — color of dividers between item groups."},"dividerThickness":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Dimension"},"dividerIndent":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Dimension","description":"Drawer-only — leading inset before each divider."},"labelStyle":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/TextStyle","description":"Default text style for item labels (selected and unselected). Per-item override via NavItem.style.labelStyle."},"iconStyle":{"type":"object","properties":{"color":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Color"},"size":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Dimension"}},"additionalProperties":false,"description":"Default icon color and size."},"selectedColor":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Color","description":"Foreground color (icon + label) for the selected item."},"unselectedColor":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Color","description":"Foreground color for non-selected items."},"elevation":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Dimension"}},"additionalProperties":false,"description":"Visual styling for a navigation surface (drawer / rail / tabs /\\nbottomBar). Every field is optional — omitted fields fall back to\\nthe active theme\'s component defaults. Used by\\n`NavigationConfig.style` (whole surface) and `NavItem.style`\\n(per-item override).\\n\\nBackgrounds compose: `backgroundColor` paints first, then\\n`backgroundImage` paints over it."},"TextStyle":{"oneOf":[{"type":"string","pattern":"^\\\\{\\\\{.*\\\\}\\\\}\$","description":"Binding expression that resolves to a TextStyle object — typically `{{theme.typography.<role>}}`."},{"type":"object","properties":{"fontFamily":{"oneOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}}]},"fontSize":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Dimension"},"fontWeight":{"anyOf":[{"type":"number"},{"type":"string","pattern":"^[1-9]00\$","description":"CSS numeric spelling (`\\"700\\"`). Documents written against CSS habits use it, and the runtime reads it the same as the number."},{"enum":["thin","extraLight","light","normal","medium","semiBold","bold","extraBold","black","regular","w100","w200","w300","w400","w500","w600","w700","w800","w900"]},{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Binding"}]},"fontStyle":{"oneOf":[{"enum":["normal","italic"]},{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Binding"}]},"color":{"type":"string"},"backgroundColor":{"type":"string"},"letterSpacing":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Dimension"},"wordSpacing":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Dimension"},"lineHeight":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Dimension","description":"Line height (05_Theme §5.4.2): below 16 a multiplier of `fontSize`, 16 and above absolute logical px. The canonical name."},"height":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Dimension","deprecated":true,"description":"Legacy name for line height, always a multiplier (§17.3.2). Accepted on input and never emitted; when `lineHeight` is also set, `lineHeight` wins (§18.2.10)."},"decoration":{"oneOf":[{"enum":["none","underline","overline","lineThrough"]},{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Binding"}]},"decorationColor":{"type":"string"},"decorationStyle":{"oneOf":[{"enum":["solid","double","dotted","dashed","wavy"]},{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Binding"}]},"decorationThickness":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Dimension"},"fontFeatures":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"},"description":"OpenType feature tags (`smcp`, `lnum`, `tnum`, `liga`, `dlig`, …)."},"shadows":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"color":{"type":"string"},"offset":{"type":"object","properties":{"dx":{"type":"number"},"dy":{"type":"number"},"x":{"type":"number"},"y":{"type":"number"}},"additionalProperties":false,"description":"`{dx, dy}` (canonical) or `{x, y}` (legacy alias) offset."},"blurRadius":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Dimension"}},"required":["color"],"additionalProperties":false}},"shader":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Gradient","description":"Gradient/shader fill applied to the rendered text via a shader mask. When set, `color` is ignored."}},"additionalProperties":true}],"description":"Inline text style applied per `text` widget instance. Layered on\\ntop of an M3 typography role when `variant` is set, or used\\nstandalone. Mirrors the theme `TextStyle` token shape (fontFamily,\\nfontSize, fontWeight, lineHeight, letterSpacing, fontFeatureSettings)\\nand adds the per-instance fields a content app needs: color,\\ndecoration, shader (gradient fill), and shadow stack.\\n\\nThe object stays open. Documents in the field carry keys this style\\nnever had — `textAlign` inside `style` is the common one, written by\\nhand before it moved onto the widget — and the runtime simply ignores\\nthem. Rejecting them here would not correct anything: validation runs\\nwhen the document loads, so a stray key inside `style` would stop the\\nwhole page instead of being ignored the way the runtime ignores it."},"Marker":{"type":"object","properties":{"latitude":{"type":"number"},"longitude":{"type":"number"},"lat":{"type":"number"},"lng":{"type":"number"},"label":{"type":"string"},"color":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Color"},"icon":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/IconRef"}},"additionalProperties":true,"description":"One point marked on a map.\\n\\nKeys the runtime reads are declared with their types; a document may carry\\nfurther keys, which the runtime ignores rather than refusing — an item shape\\nthat rejected an unknown key would break every document that carries one for\\nits own bookkeeping."},"BorderSide":{"type":"object","properties":{"color":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Color"},"width":{"type":"number","minimum":0},"style":{"enum":["solid","none"],"default":"solid"}},"additionalProperties":false,"description":"One side of a box border."},"DropCap":{"type":"object","properties":{"lines":{"type":"integer","minimum":2,"maximum":6,"default":3,"description":"Number of body-text lines the cap spans vertically."},"glyph":{"type":"string","description":"Override character. Default: first character of the text widget\'s `text`."},"style":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/TextStyle","description":"Cap-specific style overrides, layered on top of the parent widget\'s style. `fontSize` is computed from `lines × parent.fontSize` when omitted."}},"additionalProperties":false,"description":"Typographic drop-cap ornament for long-form text (book chapters,\\nmagazine articles). The first character of the text widget\'s content\\nis rendered enlarged in the top-left corner; the surrounding text\\nflows in a left-indented column for `lines` lines and then continues\\nfull width below the cap. `glyph` overrides the cap character (e.g.\\nrendering a stylised dingbat instead of the literal first letter).\\n`style` layers on top of the parent text widget\'s resolved style for\\ncap-specific overrides (typically a different `fontFamily` and\\nlarger `fontWeight`)."},"Overlay":{"type":"object","properties":{"points":{"type":"array"},"color":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Color"},"type":{"type":"string"},"width":{"type":"number"}},"additionalProperties":true,"description":"A shape drawn over a map — a path or a filled area.\\n\\nKeys the runtime reads are declared with their types; a document may carry\\nfurther keys, which the runtime ignores rather than refusing — an item shape\\nthat rejected an unknown key would break every document that carries one for\\nits own bookkeeping."},"Step":{"type":"object","properties":{"title":{"type":"string"},"titleText":{"type":"string"},"subtitle":{"type":"string"},"content":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Widget"},"state":{"type":"string"},"isActive":{"type":"boolean"}},"additionalProperties":true,"description":"One step of a stepper.\\n\\nKeys the runtime reads are declared with their types; a document may carry\\nfurther keys, which the runtime ignores rather than refusing — an item shape\\nthat rejected an unknown key would break every document that carries one for\\nits own bookkeeping."},"TimelineItem":{"type":"object","properties":{"title":{"type":"string"},"subtitle":{"type":"string"},"time":{"type":"string"},"icon":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/IconRef"},"color":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Color"}},"additionalProperties":true,"description":"One entry on a timeline.\\n\\nKeys the runtime reads are declared with their types; a document may carry\\nfurther keys, which the runtime ignores rather than refusing — an item shape\\nthat rejected an unknown key would break every document that carries one for\\nits own bookkeeping."},"TableRow":{"type":"object","properties":{"cells":{"type":"array","items":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Widget"}}},"additionalProperties":true,"description":"One row of a `table`. `cells` carries the widgets laid out across the row\'s\\ncolumns — `table` is a layout table, not a data-bound one (§10.3), so a row\\nnames its widgets rather than its values.\\n\\nNothing here is required and nothing is bounded, deliberately. `cells: []`\\ncarried a `minItems: 1` for one revision — left behind when the narrowing\\nthis file describes was reverted — and it did exactly what the paragraph\\nbelow says not to do: refused the document at load.\\n\\nNothing here is required, deliberately. A row with no `cells` — `{}`, or the\\ncolumn-keyed shape that belongs to `dataTable` (`{ \\"name\\": \\"Flutter\\" }`) —\\ncannot be laid out, and the temptation is to refuse it in the schema. That\\nrefusal happens at load, so it does not deprecate the old document, it stops\\nthe whole document opening (§1.7.5). The runtime drops the rows it cannot\\nlay out and draws the rest; the shape stays accepted."},"Sliver":{"oneOf":[{"type":"object","properties":{"type":{"const":"sliverAppBar"},"title":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Widget"},"expandedHeight":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Dimension"},"flexibleSpace":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Widget"},"background":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Widget"},"pinned":{"type":"boolean","default":false},"floating":{"type":"boolean","default":false},"snap":{"type":"boolean","default":false},"stretch":{"type":"boolean","default":false},"elevation":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Dimension"},"backgroundColor":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Color"},"foregroundColor":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Color"}},"required":["type"],"additionalProperties":false},{"type":"object","properties":{"type":{"const":"sliverPersistentHeader"},"minExtent":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Dimension"},"maxExtent":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Dimension"},"child":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Widget"},"pinned":{"type":"boolean","default":false},"floating":{"type":"boolean","default":false}},"required":["type","minExtent","maxExtent","child"],"additionalProperties":false},{"type":"object","properties":{"type":{"const":"sliverList"},"items":{"anyOf":[{"type":"array"},{"type":"string","pattern":"^\\\\{\\\\{.*\\\\}\\\\}\$"}]},"itemTemplate":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Widget"},"children":{"type":"array","items":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Widget"}}},"required":["type"],"additionalProperties":false},{"type":"object","properties":{"type":{"const":"sliverGrid"},"items":{"anyOf":[{"type":"array"},{"type":"string","pattern":"^\\\\{\\\\{.*\\\\}\\\\}\$"}]},"itemTemplate":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Widget"},"children":{"type":"array","items":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Widget"}},"columns":{"type":"number","minimum":1},"mainAxisSpacing":{"type":"number","minimum":0},"crossAxisSpacing":{"type":"number","minimum":0},"itemAspectRatio":{"type":"number","exclusiveMinimum":0}},"required":["type","columns"],"additionalProperties":false},{"type":"object","properties":{"type":{"const":"sliverFixedExtentList"},"itemExtent":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Dimension"},"items":{"anyOf":[{"type":"array"},{"type":"string","pattern":"^\\\\{\\\\{.*\\\\}\\\\}\$"}]},"itemTemplate":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Widget"},"children":{"type":"array","items":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Widget"}}},"required":["type","itemExtent"],"additionalProperties":false}],"description":"Scrollable region inside `scrollView.slivers`. Discriminated by\\n`type`:\\n\\n- **sliverAppBar** — collapsing parallax masthead at the top of a\\n  scroll view. Expands to `expandedHeight` then shrinks to a\\n  fixed bar as the user scrolls. `flexibleSpace` paints the hero\\n  area; `pinned`/`floating` control whether the bar sticks.\\n  `backgroundColor` is the colour of the **bar itself**, which is\\n  what the reader sees once the hero has faded out — without it a\\n  `title` colour chosen against the hero becomes unreadable at the\\n  moment the bar collapses, and the author has no way to say\\n  otherwise. `foregroundColor` sets the title and icon colour for\\n  the same reason.\\n- **sliverPersistentHeader** — section header that stays visible\\n  while its section\'s items scroll. `minExtent`/`maxExtent` set\\n  the size envelope; the runtime morphs the header within it.\\n- **sliverList** — vertical list with variable-height items.\\n  Same `items` + `itemTemplate` contract as the `list` widget: an inline\\n  array or a binding, either one. It accepted only the binding string for a\\n  revision, so the ordinary inline form — legal in `list` and `grid` — was\\n  refused at load in slivers alone.\\n- **sliverGrid** — 2D grid with the same `items` / `columns`\\n  contract as `grid`.\\n- **sliverFixedExtentList** — list whose items all share the\\n  same scroll-axis extent (uniform row height). Faster than\\n  `sliverList` because the runtime can skip per-item measurement.\\n\\nEach shape carries the type discriminator on `type` and is only\\nvalid inside a `scrollView.slivers` array. The runtime rejects\\nthese shapes at the top level."},"Tab":{"type":"object","properties":{"label":{"type":"string"},"text":{"type":"string"},"icon":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/IconRef"},"iconMargin":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/EdgeInsets"},"height":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Dimension"}},"additionalProperties":true,"description":"One tab of a tab bar.\\n\\nKeys the runtime reads are declared with their types; a document may carry\\nfurther keys, which the runtime ignores rather than refusing — an item shape\\nthat rejected an unknown key would break every document that carries one for\\nits own bookkeeping.\\n\\nA tab that names none of `label` / `text` / `icon` shows nothing, and that\\nis accepted: it was briefly required here, and requiring it rejects the\\ndocument at load rather than drawing an empty tab (§1.7.5). The runtime\\ndraws the empty tab."},"Span":{"oneOf":[{"type":"object","properties":{"text":{"type":"string"},"style":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/TextStyle"},"onTap":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Action"},"children":{"type":"array","items":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Span"}}},"required":["text"],"additionalProperties":false},{"type":"object","properties":{"widget":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Widget"},"alignment":{"enum":["top","middle","bottom","aboveBaseline","belowBaseline","baseline"],"default":"bottom"},"baseline":{"enum":["alphabetic","ideographic"]}},"required":["widget"],"additionalProperties":false}],"description":"Inline span in a `richText` composition. Discriminated by which\\nidentifying field is present:\\n\\n- `text` (string) → **TextSpan** — a styled run of text. Optional\\n  `style: TextStyle`, `onTap: Action`, and nested `children:\\n  Span[]` for further inline structure.\\n- `widget` (Widget) → **WidgetSpan** — an inline-widget placeholder\\n  (icon, image, custom badge) that the rich-text layout treats as\\n  a single character. `alignment` and `baseline` control its\\n  vertical placement relative to the surrounding line.\\n\\nThe two shapes are mutually exclusive — a span MUST NOT carry both\\n`text` and `widget`."},"Column":{"type":"object","properties":{"key":{"type":"string"},"field":{"type":"string"},"label":{"type":"string"},"sortable":{"type":"boolean"},"align":{"type":"string"},"width":{"type":"number"}},"additionalProperties":true,"description":"One column of a data table.\\n\\nKeys the runtime reads are declared with their types; a document may carry\\nfurther keys, which the runtime ignores rather than refusing — an item shape\\nthat rejected an unknown key would break every document that carries one for\\nits own bookkeeping."},"BoxSpacing":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string","description":"M3 spacing token resolved through `theme.spacing.<token>`. Any other string resolves to no inset and is reported at runtime."},{"type":"object","properties":{"token":{"type":"string"}},"required":["token"]},{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/EdgeInsets"}],"description":"An inset on `box`, which additionally accepts an **M3 spacing token**.\\n\\nEvery other inset slot in the DSL is a plain `EdgeInsets`. `box` is the one\\nthat also resolves a token through `theme.spacing.<token>` to a uniform\\ninset, in two spellings:\\n\\n- **Token** — `\\"md\\"`. The nine standard slots are `xxs` / `xs` / `sm` / `md`\\n  / `lg` / `xl` / `2xl` / `3xl` / `4xl`, and a theme may declare its own\\n  (`05_Theme.md` §5.5), so the form is a bare word rather than a closed set.\\n- **`{token}` object** — `{\\"token\\": \\"md\\"}`, the same lookup written as an\\n  object. Kept because it composes with the responsive override map.\\n- Everything `EdgeInsets` accepts — number, `{value, unit}`, the edge map,\\n  and a binding.\\n\\n**The string branch is deliberately open.** A value that was never a token\\n(`\\"16px\\"`, `\\"1rem\\"`) resolves to no inset, and catching it here would be\\nbetter than catching it on screen — but `box.padding` has admitted any\\nstring since 1.4, and a runtime validates documents *at load*, so\\nnarrowing this pattern would stop an already-published bundle from opening\\nrather than merely warning its author. The unresolved value is reported by\\nthe runtime instead, once per distinct value. Tightening it needs a\\nrelease allowed to break bundles; until then the report is the answer.\\n\\n`margin` takes the same spellings as `padding`. It did not until the 1.4.1\\nfollow-up — the widget has always resolved both through one helper, so the\\nnarrower declaration only made the token unauthorable, never unrenderable."},"BoxShadow":{"type":"object","properties":{"color":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Color"},"offset":{"type":"object","properties":{"dx":{"type":"number"},"dy":{"type":"number"}},"required":["dx","dy"],"additionalProperties":false},"offsetX":{"type":"number","description":"Legacy flat offset; use `offset.dx`."},"offsetY":{"type":"number","description":"Legacy flat offset; use `offset.dy`."},"blurRadius":{"type":"number","minimum":0},"blur":{"type":"number","minimum":0,"description":"Legacy alias of `blurRadius`."},"spreadRadius":{"type":"number"},"spread":{"type":"number","description":"Legacy alias of `spreadRadius`."}},"required":["color"],"additionalProperties":false,"description":"A drop shadow painted beneath the box. Multiple shadows compose via\\n`decoration.boxShadow: array<BoxShadow>` and stack from the first\\n(closest to the box) outward.\\n\\nThe offset has two spellings: `offset: {dx, dy}` (canonical) and the\\nflat `offsetX` / `offsetY` pair kept from v1.0. Likewise `blurRadius`\\nand `spreadRadius` each accept a short legacy name (`blur`, `spread`).\\nCanonical wins when both are present."},"MenuItem":{"type":"object","properties":{"value":{},"label":{"type":"string"},"icon":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/IconRef"},"enabled":{"type":"boolean"},"child":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Widget"}},"additionalProperties":true,"description":"One entry in a popup menu.\\n\\nKeys the runtime reads are declared with their types; a document may carry\\nfurther keys, which the runtime ignores rather than refusing — an item shape\\nthat rejected an unknown key would break every document that carries one for\\nits own bookkeeping."},"ExitButtonConfig":{"type":"object","properties":{"icon":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/IconRef"},"tooltip":{"type":"string"},"color":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Color"}},"additionalProperties":true,"description":"Override for the host-inserted close button.\\n\\nKeys the runtime reads are declared with their types; a document may carry\\nfurther keys, which the runtime ignores rather than refusing — an item shape\\nthat rejected an unknown key would break every document that carries one for\\nits own bookkeeping."},"BoxBorder":{"anyOf":[{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/BorderSide"},{"type":"object","properties":{"top":{"oneOf":[{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/BorderSide"},{"type":"boolean"}]},"bottom":{"oneOf":[{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/BorderSide"},{"type":"boolean"}]},"left":{"oneOf":[{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/BorderSide"},{"type":"boolean"}]},"right":{"oneOf":[{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/BorderSide"},{"type":"boolean"}]},"all":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/BorderSide"},"color":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Color"},"width":{"type":"number","minimum":0},"style":{"enum":["solid","none"]}},"additionalProperties":false}],"description":"Border around a box. Either a single uniform side applied to all four\\nedges, or per-side overrides. Per-side keys (`top` / `bottom` /\\n`left` / `right`) take precedence over `all`.\\n\\nA per-side key may also be `true`, which draws that edge with the side\\ndescribed by the sibling `color` / `width` / `style` keys — the shorthand a\\ndocument reaches for when only one edge is wanted."},"Option":{"type":"object","properties":{"value":{},"label":{"type":"string"},"binding":{"type":"string"},"icon":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/IconRef"},"enabled":{"type":"boolean"}},"required":["value"],"additionalProperties":true,"description":"One entry in a selectable list.\\n\\n`value` is required. Without it the runtime falls back to an empty string,\\nso two such entries carry the same value and selecting one selects both —\\nthe widget renders, reports nothing, and behaves wrongly. `label` falls back\\nto `value`, so the reverse substitution does not exist.\\n\\nOther keys the runtime reads are declared with their types; a document may carry\\nfurther keys, which the runtime ignores rather than refusing — an item shape\\nthat rejected an unknown key would break every document that carries one for\\nits own bookkeeping."},"DrawerItem":{"type":"object","properties":{"label":{"type":"string"},"title":{"type":"string"},"icon":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/IconRef"},"route":{"type":"string"},"value":{}},"additionalProperties":true,"description":"One entry in a drawer.\\n\\nKeys the runtime reads are declared with their types; a document may carry\\nfurther keys, which the runtime ignores rather than refusing — an item shape\\nthat rejected an unknown key would break every document that carries one for\\nits own bookkeeping."},"Point":{"type":"object","properties":{"x":{},"y":{"type":"number"},"label":{"type":"string"},"value":{"type":"number"},"color":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Color"}},"additionalProperties":true,"description":"One plotted point. `{x, y}` for a series, `{label, value}` for a category.\\n\\nKeys the runtime reads are declared with their types; a document may carry\\nfurther keys, which the runtime ignores rather than refusing — an item shape\\nthat rejected an unknown key would break every document that carries one for\\nits own bookkeeping."},"SnackBarAction":{"type":"object","properties":{"label":{"type":"string"},"onPressed":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Action"},"onTap":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Action"},"textColor":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Color"}},"additionalProperties":true,"description":"The action offered alongside a snack bar message.\\n\\nKeys the runtime reads are declared with their types; a document may carry\\nfurther keys, which the runtime ignores rather than refusing — an item shape\\nthat rejected an unknown key would break every document that carries one for\\nits own bookkeeping."},"BoxDecoration":{"type":"object","properties":{"color":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Color"},"gradient":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Gradient"},"image":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/BackgroundImage"},"border":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/BoxBorder"},"borderRadius":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/BorderRadius"},"boxShadow":{"type":"array","items":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/BoxShadow"}},"shape":{"enum":["rectangle","circle"],"default":"rectangle"},"backdropBlur":{"type":"number","minimum":0}},"additionalProperties":false,"description":"Visual decoration for a box. `color` and `gradient` are mutually\\nexclusive — when both are present `gradient` wins. `image` paints\\nbeneath the gradient/color (background image layer). `border`,\\n`borderRadius`, and `boxShadow` apply on top of the fill. `shape`\\ntoggles between rectangle (default) and circle (uses the box\'s\\nshorter side as diameter; ignores `borderRadius`). `backdropBlur`\\napplies a Gaussian blur to whatever is behind the box (for frosted-\\nglass overlays); the value is the blur sigma."},"Segment":{"type":"object","properties":{"from":{"type":"number"},"to":{"type":"number"},"color":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Color"},"label":{"type":"string"}},"additionalProperties":true,"description":"One coloured band of a gauge scale.\\n\\nKeys the runtime reads are declared with their types; a document may carry\\nfurther keys, which the runtime ignores rather than refusing — an item shape\\nthat rejected an unknown key would break every document that carries one for\\nits own bookkeeping."},"BannerAction":{"type":"object","properties":{"label":{"type":"string"},"click":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Action"},"onTap":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Action"}},"additionalProperties":true,"description":"One action offered on a banner.\\n\\nKeys the runtime reads are declared with their types; a document may carry\\nfurther keys, which the runtime ignores rather than refusing — an item shape\\nthat rejected an unknown key would break every document that carries one for\\nits own bookkeeping."},"NavItem":{"type":"object","properties":{"label":{"type":"string"},"title":{"type":"string"},"icon":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/IconRef"},"activeIcon":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/IconRef"},"backgroundColor":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Color"},"tooltip":{"type":"string"},"route":{"type":"string"}},"additionalProperties":true,"description":"One destination in a navigation surface.\\n\\nKeys the runtime reads are declared with their types; a document may carry\\nfurther keys, which the runtime ignores rather than refusing — an item shape\\nthat rejected an unknown key would break every document that carries one for\\nits own bookkeeping."},"accessibleWrapper":{"type":"object","description":"Wraps a child with accessibility annotations (ARIA-style). See [`13_Accessibility.md`](13_Accessibility.md) for the full property set.","properties":{"type":{"type":"string","enum":["accessibleWrapper"]},"click":{"anyOf":[{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Action"},{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Binding","description":"Binding expression resolving to this value."}]},"tooltip":{"description":"Hover / long-press tooltip text. Runtime wraps the widget in a\\n`Tooltip` surface.\\n","anyOf":[{"type":"string","description":"Hover / long-press tooltip text. Runtime wraps the widget in a\\n`Tooltip` surface.\\n"},{"type":"object","propertyNames":{"enum":["compact","medium","expanded","large","extraLarge","embedded","default"]},"minProperties":1,"additionalProperties":{"type":"string","description":"Hover / long-press tooltip text. Runtime wraps the widget in a\\n`Tooltip` surface.\\n"},"description":"Responsive object: one value per form factor (§14.2)."}]},"announceNavigation":{"description":"Announce navigation changes through the screen reader.","anyOf":